        [
          "python",
          "## Production-Ready Pipeline Patterns\n\nAdvanced pipelines handle real-world complexity. A typical production pipeline for tabular data:\n\n1. **Imputation**: Handle missing values using KNNImputer (preserves relationships)\n2. **Scaling**: StandardScaler or MinMaxScaler depending on algorithms\n3. **Encoding**: OneHotEncoder for low-cardinality categoricals, TargetEncoder for high-cardinality\n4. **Feature engineering**: Create interactions, polynomials, or domain-specific features\n5. **Outlier handling**: Remove or cap extreme values (optional)\n6. **Feature selection**: Remove noise and redundant features\n7. **Dimensionality reduction**: Optional; reduces overfitting or speeds training\n8. **Modeling**: Classification, regression, or clustering\n\nEach step is testable independently. Unit tests verify each transformer behaves correctly. Integration tests verify the full pipeline works end-to-end.\n\n## Estimator Validation and Testing\n\nWhen building production pipelines, validate each component:"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "This runs ~200 internal tests on the transformer, ensuring it follows sklearn's contract. Critical for pipelines to work reliably.\n\n## Saving Preprocessing State\n\nPreprocessing state (like scaler means or encoder mappings) must be reproducible. Always save the entire fitted pipeline:"
        ]
      ]
